```jsx
import React, { useState } from 'react';

const Autocomplete = ({ suggestions, onSelect }) => {
  const [input, setInput] = useState('');
  const [activeSuggestion, setActiveSuggestion] = useState(-1);

  const filteredSuggestions = suggestions.filter(
    (suggestion) =>
      suggestion.toLowerCase().includes(input.toLowerCase()) &&
      parseFloat(suggestion) === parseFloat(input)
  );

  const handleInputChanged = (event) => {
    setInput(event.target.value);
  };

  const handleSuggestionsClicked = (index) => {
    setActiveSuggestion(-1);
    onSelect(filteredSuggestions[index]);
  };

  const handleKeyDown = (event) => {
    if (event.key === 'ArrowDown') {
      if (activeSuggestion < filteredSuggestions.length - 1) {
        setActiveSuggestion(activeSuggestion + 1);
      }
    }
    if (event.key === 'ArrowUp') {
      if (activeSuggestion > 0) {
        setActiveSuggestion(activeSuggestion - 1);
      }
    }
    if (event.key === 'Enter') {
      if (activeSuggestion >= 0) {
        onSelect(filteredSuggestions[activeSuggestion]);
      }
    }
  };

  const handleBlur = () => {
    setTimeout(() => {
      setActiveSuggestion(-1);
    }, 100);
  };

  if (input && filteredSuggestions.length > 0) {
    return (
      <div className="autocomplete-suggestions">
        <ul>
          {filteredSuggestions.map((suggestion, index) => (
            <li
              key={index}
              className={
                'suggestion ' +
                (activeSuggestion === index ? 'active' : '')
              }
              onClick={() => handleSuggestionsClicked(index)}
            >
              {suggestion}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    );
  } else {
    return <input type="text" value={input} onChange={handleInputChanged} onKeyDown={handleKeyDown} onBlur={handleBlur} />;
  }
};

export default Autocomplete;
```

In this code, we use the `useState` hook to track the current input value and the currently active suggestion. We also maintain an `onSelect` callback function that gets called when a suggestion is selected.

The `handleInputChanged` function updates the input value whenever the user types something.

The `handleSuggestionsClicked` function updates the `activeSuggestion` state and calls the `onSelect` function when a suggestion is clicked.

The `handleKeyDown` function handles key presses and updates the `activeSuggestion` state and calls the `onSelect` function when the Enter key is pressed.

The `handleBlur` function resets the `activeSuggestion` state when the input loses focus.

